theta\\right)$, with $Y_0$ and $Y_1$ the Bessel functions of the second kind at $t$, checked to solve this spacetime's own field equations; as $t \\to 0$, $P \\to \\tfrac{1}{2}\\cos\\theta\\,\\tau$ with $\\tau = -\\ln t$.","caption":["The plane of $t$ and $\\theta$ ($\\sigma = 0$, $\\delta = 0$) of a polarised wave on the torus, the edges $\\theta = 0$ and $\\theta = 2\\pi$ one line. The metric on it is $L^2t^{-1/2}e^{\\lambda/2}(-dt^2 + d\\theta^2)$, and the factor drops out of the null condition, so for every wave the rays are at 45°. No Christoffel symbol turns them out of the plane, so they are null geodesics.","A ray leaving the singularity $t = 0$ has covered the angle $t$ by the time $t$, so two events at the time $t$ whose $\\theta$ differ by more than $2t$ have no event in both their pasts, and a ray first comes back to its own $\\theta$ at $t = 2\\pi$."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains","einstein_tensor"],"version":"1cb6ac6bea3b0305"},"slices":[{"view":"torus","surface":0,"label":"$t = 0.25$","version":"0ecb278cdf51b9eb","lines":[[[0.0,0.0398],[1.0,0.0398]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.0398],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"torus","surface":1,"label":"$t = 0.5$","version":"e15f0aa20a7b6788","lines":[[[0.0,0.0796],[1.0,0.0796]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.0,0.0796],"anchor":"bl","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"torus","surface":2,"label":"$t = 1$","version":"2b6da18427ae478c","lines":[[[0.0,0.1592],[1.0,0.1592]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.1592],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"torus","surface":3,"label":"$t = 2$","version":"91b525fa456eef14","lines":[[[0.0,0.3183],[1.0,0.3183]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.3183],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"torus","surface":4,"label":"$t = 3$","version":"cf55cd25bc13897e","lines":[[[0.0,0.4775],[1.0,0.4775]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.4775